###  http://www.semanticweb.org/jluis/ontologies/sdco#BDE
:BDE rdf:type owl:Class ;
     owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                           owl:onProperty <https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#hasConditionCode> ;
                           owl:hasValue "BDE"
                         ] ;
     rdfs:subClassOf :PipeOther ,
                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                       owl:onProperty :hasPipeFeature ;
                       owl:someValuesFrom :FlowFromIncomingPipe
                     ] ;
     rdfs:comment """Flow from incoming pipe

Information about the wastewater flowing from an incoming pipe.\"  Where this is used the item for a connection (Code BCA) is also required.

The wastewater flowing from the incoming pipe is:  
- clear effluent (the invert of the incoming pipe is visible) (A);  
- use of code discontinued (B);  
- turbid (C);  
- coloured (D); 
- turbid and coloured (E).  
- If the wastewater flowing from the incoming pipe is not visible because the water level in the main pipe is too high the characterisation code YY shall be used""" .


