###  https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Component
<https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Component> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:comment """Die Komponententaxonomie umfasst die Hauptkomponenten eines Kanalisationssystems gemäß dem Merkblatt DWA-M 150 und der Referenztabelle 128 \"Objekttypen\".

Es wird empfohlen, Individuen für Haltungsabschnitte mit der Vorlage zu erstellen:

PipeSection[PipeSectionDesignation]
PipeSection[HG001]

Es wird empfohlen, Individuen für Knoten mit der Vorlage zu erstellen:

Node[NodeDesignation]
Node[KG001]

Es wird ebenfalls empfohlen, zu deklarieren, dass Komponenten zu einer anderen Komponente mit der asymmetrischen/ irreflexiven Unterobjekteigenschaft flowsTo (Invers: flowsFrom) fließen.

Die Ontologie sollte dann automatisch folgern, dass alle Komponenten, die zu/von einander fließen, verbunden sind — mit ihrer transitiven Überobjekteigenschaft \"connectedWith\".

Revision 1 Aug 2025: NodeStructure wurde als Unterklasse von Node hinzugefügt. Diese Strukturen reflektieren <KA> innerhalb einer M150-XML-Datei."""@de ,
                                                              """The taxonomy of components includes the main components of a sewage system according to the advisory leaflet DWA-M 150 and the reference table 128 \"Object Types\".

It is recommended to create individuals for Pipe Sections with the template:

` PipeSection[PipeSectionDesignation] `
` PipeSection[HG001] `

It is recommended to create individuals for Nodes with the template:

` Node[NodeDesignation] `
` Node[KG001] `

It is also recommended to declare that Components flows to another component with the asymmetric/irreflexive sub-object property `flowsTo` (Inverse: flowsFrom).

The ontology should then automatically reason, that all components flowing to / from each other are connected -- with its transitive super-object property \"connectedWith\".

Revision 1 Aug 2025: NodeStructure added as a Subclass of Node. These structures reflect <KA> within an M150-XML."""@en ;
                                                 rdfs:label "Component"@en ,
                                                            "Komponente"@de .


###  https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Condition
<https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Condition> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Inspection> .


###  https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Inspection
<https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Inspection> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Report> .


###  https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Node
<https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Node> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Component> ;
                                            owl:disjointWith <https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#PipeSection> ;
                                            rdfs:comment """A node is a component in a sewage system that serves as a junction for pipes. It's often where manholes or access points are located.

It is recommended to create individuals for Nodes with the template:

` Node[NodeDesignation] `
` Node[KG001] `"""@en ;
                                            rdfs:label "Knote"@de ,
                                                       "Node"@en .


###  https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#PipeSection
<https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#PipeSection> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Component> .


###  https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Report
<https://l-jamora.github.io/m150-onto#Report> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:comment """The taxonomy of reports includes inspection and condition reports for a sewage system, according to the structure of the advisory leaflet DWA-M 150.

It is recommended to create individuals for inspection reports with the template:

` Inspection[PipeSectionDesignation]_[Date] `;
` Inspection[HG001]_[HI003] ` for Pipe Section: Inspection reports;
` Inspection[KG001]_[KI003] ` for Node: Inspection reports.

It is recommended to create individuals for condition reports within an inspection with the template:

` Condition[PipeSectionDesignation]_[Stationing(ConditionReport)]_[Code] `;
` Condition[HG001]_[HZ001]_[HZ002] ` for Pipe Section: Condition reports;
` Condition[HG001]_[KZ001]_[KZ002] ` for Node: Condition reports.

According to the DWA-M 150, the coding systems that can be applied here are:
- DIN EN 13508-2
- DWA 149-2
- DWA ATV-M 143
- ISYBAU2001
- ISYBAU1996"""@en .


